Value PORT (\S+)
Value NAME (\S.*\S|\S)
Value STATUS (connected|notconnect|inactive|errdisabled|disabled)
Value VLAN_ID (\S+)
Value DUPLEX (\S+)
Value SPEED (\S+)
Value TYPE (Not\s+Present|\S+)
Value FLAGS (\S+)
Value LINK_SPEED (\d+(?:\.\d+)?[MG])

Start
  ^${PORT}(?:\s+${NAME})?\s+${STATUS}\s+(?:in\s+)?${VLAN_ID}\s+${DUPLEX}\s+${SPEED}\s+${TYPE}(?:\s+${FLAGS})?(?:\s+\S+)?\s*$$ -> Continue
  # LINK_SPEED is the speed the port runs at: only on a connected port, negotiated (a-1G) or forced
  # (1G), and a port-channel's is the sum of its members (2G). A port that is not up, or whose Speed
  # column is not a number (auto, unconf), has none (#57). Same greedy Name as the rule above.
  ^\S+(?:\s+\S.*)?\s+connected\s+(?:in\s+)?\S+\s+\S+\s+(?:a-)?${LINK_SPEED}\s+(?:Not\s+Present|\S+)(?:\s+\S+)?(?:\s+\S+)?\s*$$ -> Record
  ^${PORT}(?:\s+${NAME})?\s+${STATUS}\s+(?:in\s+)?${VLAN_ID}\s+${DUPLEX}\s+${SPEED}\s+${TYPE}(?:\s+${FLAGS})?(?:\s+\S+)?\s*$$ -> Record
  ^Port\s+Name\s+Status\s+Vlan\s+Duplex\s+Speed\s+Type(?:\s+Flags)?(?:\s+Encapsulation)?\s*$$
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error
